  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.test-coverage.index.render_only`. I judged them from the supplied test source and did not request implementation source. The subject has three obligations, and the tests cover each one.\n\n**Rendered from source annotations and stored review results**\n- `src/execution_coverage/book.rs#mod[tests]/fn[overview_shows_missing_unreadable_and_recorded_reviews_with_current_justifications]` writes a source file with a `{cite}` annotation and a `///` justification.\n- It then renders under each stored-review state: missing, true, false, FIXME, invalid JSON, and unreadable (a directory in place of the file).\n- It asserts the \"Recorded review: <strong>{label}</strong>\" label, the saved rationale, the FIXME text, and the \"invalid JSON\" and \"cannot read evidence\" diagnostics. It also asserts the current source justification and the \"1 documented source items\" count.\n- It edits the source so the justification text changes or disappears. The rendered overview then shows the updated justification or \"No tracked justification is present.\"\n\n**Without reading saved execution measurements**\n- `book_ignores_saved_measurements_and_preserves_artifacts` first renders a book with no saved attempts and keeps that as the baseline.\n- It then records an attempt with coverage hits and a distinctive test name, and renders again. The chapters must be identical to the baseline. The test name must not appear. The `<select`, \"Line coverage:\", \"Captured source\", \"Test runs and provenance\" and \"0 unresolved gaps\" markers must not appear. The chapter names and paths must not change.\n- It then corrupts `attempt.json`, once as invalid metadata and once as `{}`. The output stays identical to the baseline. The metadata file and `.profraw` are untouched, and no `selection-cache.json` is created. Together these show the measurements are neither read nor altered.\n- `tests/execution_coverage.rs#fn[book_rendering_preserves_retained_coverage_and_never_launches_tests]` runs `habeas mdbook` end to end after a real coverage capture. A wrapper `cargo` records its calls and fails on any command other than `metadata`. The test asserts that only `metadata` calls occur, that no forbidden command ran, that the test-execution sentinel is absent, and that the retained coverage files are byte-identical. This also covers the cited `requirements.index.render_only` obligations not to run tests, collect coverage, or load measurements.\n\n**Without evaluating exception acceptance or auditing review freshness**\n- The overview test stores reviews with `\"hash\": \"old hash\"` and empty inputs. After the source changes, it also keeps a bare review with no hash or inputs.\n- It asserts that the stored review is still shown as \"Recorded true\", false, or FIXME with its saved rationale. It asserts the output never contains \"current and accepted\" or \"input is stale\". It asserts the review file bytes are unchanged and that no `target` directory is created.\n- This shows no acceptance verdict and no freshness check is applied. A FIXME or false determination is displayed as recorded rather than being evaluated.\n\n**Cited `index.render_only` read and parse failures**\nThe invalid JSON and unreadable review cases produce readable diagnostics in the overview. The rendering call still succeeds with `unwrap()`, so these failures are not turned into a validation verdict.\n\nI found no unacknowledged gap. All three tests carry `{test}` references to the subject.",
